# deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore — what the image build (deploy/Dockerfile, context: the repository root) never sees.
#
# Why:   a smaller context builds faster, and local files must never reach an image: `.env` files with development
#        values, fetched or generated folders (the image gets H5P core, editor and the content types only through
#        the checked build contexts, D-110), test trees and documentation.
# Spec:  NFR-007
# Tests: tools/deploy-check/test/deployFiles.test.mjs (that `.env` files and the fetched folders stay out).
# SECURITY: `.env` and `.env.*` anywhere, and `.git`, are excluded first and never re-included.

**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
.github
.husky
.devcontainer
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
apps/server/var
apps/server/h5p
apps/server/src/generated
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
apps/server/test
apps/server/e2e
apps/server/a11y
apps/web/test
packages/*/test
deploy
docs
!docs/reference/h5p-core-1.28-seed-packages/*.files.sha256
tools
!tools/h5p-core/verifyClientFiles.mjs
!tools/h5p-libraries/resolveManifest.mjs
!tools/h5p-bundle/contentTypeBundle.mjs
!tools/h5p-bundle/bundleCli.mjs
